  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000121968,
      "SummaryText": "Executive Summary \nONEOK Bridgeport Processing Plant is in Wise County, Texas, approximately three miles \nsouthwest of Bridgeport, TX. Its coordinates are 33.19592\u00b0N, -97.80311\u00b0W. The address for the \nfacility is 415 Private Road 3502, Bridgeport, TX76426.\nBridgeport Processing Plant is a fractionating NGL plant consist of seven natural gas processing \ntrains designed for 720 MMSCFD / 15000 BBLs/Day. Although current throughput through \nBridgeport Plant is reduced to 400 MMSCFD to 500 MMSCFD with five natural gas processing \ntrains in operation. The facility consists of inlet separation and filtration, amine gas treating and \nregeneration, glycol gas treating and regeneration, molecular sieve dehydration and regeneration, cryogenic processing units, refrigeration compressors, condensate stabilization, residue compression, hot oil systems, and all associated utilities and ancillary systems. Treated natural gas from residue compression are sent offsite via pipeline. The products from fractionation plant such as propane, butanes, gasoline, condensate are stored in various tanks located in the tank farm.. \nBridgeport Plant (or Facility) is subject to 40 CFR Part 68 because it consists of more than the \nthreshold quantity of a \u0093regulated flammable substance (10,000 pounds)\u0094. The total regulated \nflammable substance at the facility is 12,415,378 lbs. (including piping, 10% equipment inventory) plus 221,528 lbs. of methanol. The Facility does not store any toxic substances above threshold quantities. \nThe table below lists the regulated substances.\nTable 1: Covered Chemical\nRegulated Substance CAS Number\nButane 106-97-8\nEthane 74-84-0\nIsobutane 75-28-5\nIsopentane 78-78-4\nMethane 74-82-8\nPentane 109-66-0\nPropane 74-98-6\nThe Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) Risk Management Plan (RMP) rule defines three \nprogram levels based on processes\u0092 relative potential for public impacts and the level of efforts needed to prevent accidents. For each Program level, the rule defines r"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000121968,
      "SummaryText": "equirements that reflect the level of risk and effort associated with the processes at that level.\nBridgeport Plant was determined to be Program Level 3. The facility is not eligible for Program \nlevel 1 as the public receptors (residential unit) are located within the distance to endpoint of 1 psi overpressure from a vapor cloud explosion in worst case release scenario. In addition, Bridgeport facility is not eligible for Program level 2 because the facility is subject to OSHA PSM standard."
    }
  ]
